window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-71293722d815f9b8"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"get-started-with-chatgpt-space\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-space\">开始使用 ChatGPT Space</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以根据笔记、文件或对话创建页面或幻灯片。你需要一个已启用 Space 的账户。</p> <p><a id=\"open-space\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"space\">打开 Space</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 中打开 <strong>Space</strong>。<strong>All（全部）</strong>会汇集你保存的工作。使用 <strong>Your items（你的内容）</strong>查找自己的内容，使用 <strong>Shared with you（与你共享）</strong>查看他人共享的内容，也可以按名称搜索。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Space 中的 All（全部）视图，包含 Suggested（建议）、Favorites（收藏）、Your items（你的内容）和 Shared with you（与你共享）选项卡、搜索框和 New（新建）菜单。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"draft-your-first-page\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">起草你的第一个页面</h2> <ol> <li>创建页面</li> </ol> <p>在侧边栏中选择 <strong>New page（新建页面）</strong>。为页面命名并开始输入、粘贴笔记或添加文件。你也可以请 ChatGPT 根据已有对话创建页面。</p> <ol> <li>添加上下文</li> </ol> <p>添加你希望 ChatGPT 使用的笔记、文件或链接。如果资料位于 Google Drive 等应用中，请先连接该应用，再指定相关文件。</p> <ol> <li>请 ChatGPT 协助</li> </ol> <p>在页面旁打开 ChatGPT，描述你想制作的内容。你可以复制下面的提示词来整理零散笔记：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">将本页笔记整理成一份清晰的草稿。在适当位置使用标题和项目符号。保留事实和来源链接，并在末尾列出所有尚待解答的问题。\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>编辑结果</li> </ol> <p>直接修改文本，或让 ChatGPT 继续修订。共享前，请在页面中检查结果。</p> <p><a id=\"create-and-refine-slides\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">创建并完善幻灯片</h2> <p>ChatGPT Slides 可以让你与团队和 ChatGPT 一起在 Space 中制作演示文稿。在移动设备上，你可以通过对话创建幻灯片并查看演示文稿；要直接编辑幻灯片元素，请使用网页端或桌面应用。</p> <ol> <li>从现有材料开始</li> </ol> <p>请 ChatGPT 根据对话、大纲或源文件，在 Space 中创建演示文稿。说明受众、目标和篇幅。你也可以提供参考演示文稿或模板，以指导版式和风格。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用这些笔记和指标，在 Space 中创建一份包含 8 张幻灯片的季度业务回顾。受众是我们的领导团队。涵盖成果、风险和需要作出决策的事项。将附带的演示文稿作为风格参考，保留源数据中的数字，并标出缺失的信息。\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>完善演示文稿</li> </ol> <p>在 Space 中打开可编辑的演示文稿。你可以直接编辑文字、图片、形状、表格和图表，也可以选择某个元素并点击 <strong>Request edits（请求修改）</strong>让 ChatGPT 修改。对于整份演示文稿的调整（例如缩短内容，以适合高管受众），可以使用提示词栏。你也可以让 ChatGPT 生成图片，或使用你上传的视觉素材。</p> <ol> <li>与团队协作</li> </ol> <p>共享演示文稿并授予协作者编辑权限，让大家同时修改同一份幻灯片。你可以使用共享评论讨论反馈，也可以提及队友、ChatGPT 或你的 dot 来请求修改。有关权限和反馈，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=collaborate-on-slides\">协作制作幻灯片</a>。</p> <ol> <li>演示或导出</li> </ol> <p>演示前请检查事实、图表和版式。你可以在 ChatGPT 中直接演示并使用演讲者备注，也可以导出演示文稿。在网页端，你可以导出为 PowerPoint（<code>.pptx</code>）、PDF 或 Google Slides。在桌面应用中，如果已安装 PowerPoint 或 Keynote，还会出现使用这些应用打开演示文稿的选项。共享前，请检查导出文件的内容和格式。</p> <p>如果 Windows 桌面应用创建的是 PowerPoint 文件，而不是协作式演示文稿，请切换到云模式，或使用 ChatGPT 网页版在 Space 中创建和编辑幻灯片。</p> <p><a id=\"group-related-pages-in-a-space\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"space_1\">在 Space 中归类相关页面</h2> <p>如果某个主题或团队有多个相关页面，可以创建一个 Space。从 <strong>All（全部）</strong>打开 <strong>New（新建）</strong>并选择 <strong>Space</strong>。填写主题或群组名称；如有需要，可以展开 <strong>Invite people（邀请人员）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Create（创建）</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：创建 Space 的对话框，其中包含名称栏、Invite people（邀请人员）选项，以及 Cancel（取消）和 Create（创建）按钮。</p> </blockquote> <p>受邀加入 Space 的人员可以访问其中的页面。若只想共享单个页面，请使用该页面的共享设置。有关权限，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=understand-inherited-access\">继承的访问权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"review-and-share\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">审阅和共享</h2> <ol> <li>打开页面的共享设置。</li> <li>选择要邀请的人员或可用团队，并设置权限。只需阅读时选择查看权限；需要共同修改页面时选择编辑权限。</li> <li>共享链接。协作者可以打开页面；如果拥有编辑权限，还可以与你和 ChatGPT 一起修改内容。</li> </ol>","en":"<h1 id=\"get-started-with-chatgpt-space\">Get started with ChatGPT Space</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Create a page or slide deck from notes, files, or a conversation. You need an account with Space enabled.</p> <h2 id=\"open-space\">Open Space</h2> <p>Open <strong>Space</strong> in ChatGPT. <strong>All</strong> brings together your saved work. Use <strong>Your items</strong> to find your own content, <strong>Shared with you</strong> for content others have shared, or search by name.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The All view in Space, with Suggested, Favorites, Your items, and Shared with you tabs, a search field, and a New menu.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"draft-your-first-page\">Draft your first page</h2> <ol> <li>Create a page</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>New page</strong> in the sidebar. Give it a title and start typing, paste your notes, or add a file. You can also ask ChatGPT to create a page from an existing conversation.</p> <ol> <li>Add context</li> </ol> <p>Include the notes, files, or links you want ChatGPT to use. For content in an app such as Google Drive, connect the app and point ChatGPT to the relevant files.</p> <ol> <li>Ask ChatGPT to help</li> </ol> <p>Open ChatGPT alongside the page and describe what you want to make. Copy this prompt to organize rough notes:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Organize the notes on this page into a clear draft. Use headings and bullet points where they help. Preserve the facts and source links, and list any open questions at the end.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Edit the result</li> </ol> <p>Change the text directly or ask ChatGPT for a revision. Check the result on the page before sharing it.</p> <h2 id=\"create-and-refine-slides\">Create and refine slides</h2> <p>ChatGPT Slides lets you build a presentation with your team and ChatGPT in Space. On mobile, you can create slides through conversation and view decks. Use the web or desktop to edit slide elements directly.</p> <ol> <li>Start with your material</li> </ol> <p>Ask ChatGPT to create a presentation in Space from a conversation, an outline, or source files. Describe the audience, goal, and length. You can also provide a reference deck or template to guide the layout and style.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create an 8-slide quarterly business review in Space using these notes and metrics. The audience is our leadership team. Cover results, risks, and decisions needed. Use the attached deck as a style reference, preserve the source numbers, and flag missing information.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Refine the deck</li> </ol> <p>Open the editable deck in Space. Edit text, images, shapes, tables, and charts directly, or select an element and choose <strong>Request edits</strong> to ask ChatGPT for a change. Use the prompt bar for changes across the deck, such as shortening the story for an executive audience. Ask ChatGPT to generate images or use visuals you upload.</p> <ol> <li>Work with your team</li> </ol> <p>Share the deck and give collaborators edit access to work on the same slides at the same time. Use shared comments to discuss changes or mention ChatGPT or your dot to request a revision. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=collaborate-on-slides\">Collaborate on slides</a> for permissions and feedback.</p> <ol> <li>Present or export</li> </ol> <p>Check the facts, charts, and layout before presenting. Present directly in ChatGPT with speaker notes, or export the deck. On the web, you can export to PowerPoint (<code>.pptx</code>), PDF, or Google Slides. In the desktop app, options to open the deck in PowerPoint or Keynote appear when those apps are installed. Review the exported deck's content and formatting before sharing it.</p> <p>If the Windows desktop app creates a PowerPoint file instead of a collaborative deck, switch to cloud mode or use ChatGPT on the web to create and edit slides in Space.</p> <h2 id=\"group-related-pages-in-a-space\">Group related pages in a space</h2> <p>For a topic or team with related pages, create a space. From <strong>All</strong>, open <strong>New</strong> and select <strong>Space</strong>. Name the topic or group, optionally expand <strong>Invite people</strong>, then select <strong>Create</strong>. You can share the space later.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Create a space dialog with a name field, an Invite people option, and Cancel and Create actions.</p> </blockquote> <p>People invited to a space receive access to its pages. To share only one page, use that page's sharing controls instead. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=understand-inherited-access\">inherited access</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"review-and-share\">Review and share</h2> <ol> <li>Open the page's sharing controls.</li> <li>Choose a person or an available team and set their permission. Use view access for readers or edit access to work on the page together.</li> <li>Share the link. Collaborators can open the page and, with edit access, make changes alongside you and ChatGPT.</li> </ol>"};
